the queue trailed out of the hospital  gates and down the street the stark  warning of an imminent tidal wave of  omicron prompting a massive surge of  vaccine uptake at hundreds of  vaccination centers across the uk  the prime minister visited a vaccination  center to see the work firsthand and  broke the news of the uk's first omicron  related death omicron is producing  hospitalizations and  sadly at least one patient has now  been confirmed to have died  with omicron so  i think the idea that this is somehow a  milder version of the virus i think  that's something we need to set on one  side and just recognize the sheer  pace at which it accelerates through the  population the mission to offer millions  of booster jabs by december 31st will  see 42 military planning teams deployed  across every health region extra vaccine  sites and mobile units extended clinic  opening hours to allow people to be  jabbed around the clock and at weekends  and the training of thousands more  volunteer vaccinators  hitting the government's target would  mean one million jabs being put into  people's arms every single day between  now and the end of december and that's  never been achieved before currently the  nhs is managing around half of that but  the importance of trying has been  emphasized by new modelling which shows  that in some circumstances omicron could  cause double the number of  hospitalizations that delta did a year  ago  and the booster jab gives 70 protection  against infection  new rules on wearing masks and working  from home have now also come into effect  in england passenger numbers on public  transport have dropped significantly and  many businesses are cancelling their  end-of-year parties but there are  determined pockets of political and  public resistance to new restrictions  i've been speaking to a lot of people i  don't think that the compliance will be  as high as it has been in past lockdowns  simply because  we've had this stint of  basically no restrictions  with the christmas holiday less than two  weeks away it's going to be a race  against time to avoid even more  stringent restrictions paul brennan al  jazeera london
 

